What is LocalStorage?

LocalStorage is a feature of the browser that allows a website to store data on the user's computer.
The data is saved as key–value pairs and remains stored even after the page is refreshed or the browser is closed.

It is part of the Web Storage API in JavaScript.

📌 Example:
A website can remember:

Dark mode preference

User notes

Login information

Shopping cart items

Characteristics of LocalStorage

Data is stored in key–value format

Data persists after refresh

Data does not expire automatically

Only strings can be stored

Storage limit is about 5–10 MB depending on browser

Example:

localStorage.setItem("username", "Sudha");

Here:

Key = "username"

Value = "Sudha"

Basic LocalStorage Functions
1. setItem()

This function stores data in localStorage.

Syntax

localStorage.setItem(key, value);

Example

localStorage.setItem("name", "Sudha");

This saves the name Sudha in the browser storage.

2. getItem()

This function retrieves data from localStorage.

Syntax

localStorage.getItem(key);

Example

let name = localStorage.getItem("name");
console.log(name);

Output:

Sudha
3. removeItem()

This function removes a specific item from localStorage.

Syntax

localStorage.removeItem(key);

Example

localStorage.removeItem("name");

Now the name value is deleted from storage.

4. clear()

This function removes all data stored in localStorage.

Syntax

localStorage.clear();

Example:

localStorage.clear();

This deletes everything stored in localStorage.

Example Program
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>LocalStorage Example</title>
</head>

<body>

<button onclick="saveData()">Save Name</button>
<button onclick="getData()">Get Name</button>
<button onclick="deleteData()">Delete Name</button>

<script>

function saveData(){
localStorage.setItem("name","Sudha");
}

function getData(){
let name = localStorage.getItem("name");
alert(name);
}

function deleteData(){
localStorage.removeItem("name");
}

</script>

</body>
</html>
Summary
Function	Purpose
setItem()	Store data
getItem()	Retrieve data
removeItem()	Delete one item
clear()	Delete all stored data
